{"title":"Why is Milei begging for a bailout?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/925387238/0/marginalrevolution~Why-is-Milei-begging-for-a-bailout.html","date":1758874236000,"content":"<p>There are two primary reasons.</p>\r\n<p>First, he pegged Argentina’s real exchange rate too high, hoping this would appease voters by getting inflation down more quickly.  That was a miscalculation.  It also was a violation of market or libertarian principles.  The problems here are not an instance of market failure, rather Milei forgot his own principles.</p>\r\n<p>Second, the opposition did very well in a recent election.  So everyone is afraid the reign of Milei, or like-minded leaders, is not going to last for so long.  That precipitated a crisis in the markets.  But that is hardly an argument against Milei, even though it happened on his watch.  It is an argument against the likely alternatives to Milei.</p>\r\n<p>So it is a mistake to read recent events as somehow a repudiation of market or libertarian principles.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/why-is-milei-begging-for-a-bailout.html\">Why is Milei begging for a bailout?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/925387238/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/925387238/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/925387238/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/925387238/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.co